  "releaseNotes": "v0.1.6-preview: Structured Tool Parameters\n\nNew Features:\n- Structured Tool Parameters: attribute-based type-safe tool parameter definition with automatic validation and JSON schema generation\n- ToolParameterAttribute for defining parameters with constraints (Required, MinimumValue, MaximumValue, MinLengthValue, MaxLengthValue, Enum, Pattern, DefaultValue, Description)\n- ToolParameterMetadata for reflection-based extraction of parameter definitions from tool properties\n- ToolParameterSchema for JSON schema generation enabling LLM understanding of parameter requirements\n- ToolParameterBinder for automatic parsing, validation, and type-safe binding of tool arguments\n- Comprehensive validation: enum values, numeric ranges, string length, regex patterns, required parameters\n- Automatic error handling: validation errors sent back to LLM with descriptive messages\n- StructuredTools sample demonstrating realistic use cases (calculator, hotel search, hotel booking)\n- Backward compatible: optional opt-in feature, existing string-based tools work unchanged\n\nImprovements:\n- Agent.ReplyAsync() integrates parameter binding before tool invocation\n- Tool catalog messages now include parameter schemas for LLM clarity\n- 17 comprehensive unit tests with 100% pass rate\n- Full documentation and README\n\nBreaking Changes: None\n\nSupported Constraint Types:\n- Numeric: MinimumValue, MaximumValue for int, long, double, float, decimal\n- String: MinLengthValue, MaxLengthValue, Enum values, Pattern (regex)\n- Required: mark parameters that must be provided\n- Type Support: string, int, long, double, float, decimal, short, byte, bool, arrays, lists\n\nSee: samples/StructuredTools/README.md for complete documentation and examples",
